<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Omar Ali Saifuddien Mosque</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1958">1958</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Omar Ali Saifuddien Mosque is a royal mosque in Bandar Seri Begawan, the capital of Brunei, completed in 1958 and named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omar-ali-saifuddien-iii">Omar Ali Saifuddien III</a>. Standing beside an artificial lagoon near the water village of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampong-ayer">Kampong Ayer</a>, it has a golden dome and a tall minaret, and a replica of a royal barge stands in the lagoon. It is one of the best-known buildings in South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/omar-ali-saifuddien-mosque.jpg" alt="Omar Ali Saifuddien Mosque" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abdullah Geelah · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sultan_Omar_Ali_Saifuddin_Mosque_with_the_ceremonial_ship.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
